\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Is there one uniform bounded-error classical logarithmic-word RAM algorithm for positive-integer Subset Sum which, for every fixed c, uses at most $C_c$ $2^{0.49n}$ operations on every random path whenever its n items have bit length $b\leq n^c$, and is correct with probability $\geq 2/3$ without being given c?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Is there one uniform bounded-error classical logarithmic-word RAM algorithm for positive-integer Subset Sum which, for every fixed c, uses at most $C_c$ $2^{0.49n}$ operations on every random path whenever its n items have bit length $b\leq n^c$, and is correct with probability $\geq 2/3$ without being given c?

