\section*{Worst-case Subset Sum below the half exponent}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 138; 2026-10-04), the asserted result is that bounded-error classical Subset Sum on polynomial-bit inputs has a uniform $O(2^{0.49n})$ algorithm with that bound on every random execution.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 138; 2026-10-04), filtered representations recover modular aliases through small digit lists. Input-independent pair scores satisfy weighted Fourier-moment bounds, and checksum estimation combines direct sums with importance sampling; deterministic caps control both the visited lists and numerical work.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 138; 2026-10-04).

\subsection{Formal verification}
